  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "M3YurfhG2gkqgyETNp9c3EMDH84=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:38:09.499Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Editors and drive apps declare their behaviour by writing into a global config store, and the setters come in two flavours: imperative (`setPH\u2026Config`) and mount-time (`useSetPH\u2026Config`).\n\nTwo config slices matter here:\n\n```ts\nexport type PHAppConfig = {\n  /** Empty array means any document type is allowed. */\n  allowedDocumentTypes?: string[];\n  isDragAndDropEnabled?: boolean;\n};\n\nexport type PHDocumentEditorConfig = {\n  isExternalControlsEnabled?: boolean;\n};\n```\n\nBoth are members of the larger `PHGlobalConfig` intersection, and `setPHAppConfig` / `setPHDocumentEditorConfig` simply iterate the partial's keys and forward each one to the per-key global setter \u2014 so setting a slice is exactly equivalent to setting its keys individually.\n\nThe wrapper hooks are what codegen actually emits. The app template writes `useSetPHAppConfig(editorConfig)` at the top of the generated editor, with the object living in a sibling `./config.ts`. Read the implementation before relying on it: the hook guards its effect with a one-shot `isInitialized` state flag, so it applies the config **once on mount and never again**. Passing a config object that changes between renders will not update anything \u2014 for dynamic changes call the imperative `setPHAppConfig` directly.\n\n**Naming caveat \u2014 the academy is stale here.** `04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md` documents `PHDriveEditorConfig`, `setPHDriveEditorConfig` and `useSetPHDriveEditorConfig`. Those identifiers have **zero occurrences** anywhere in the monorepo outside build output; the slice was renamed to `PHAppConfig` and the functions to `setPHAppConfig` / `useSetPHAppConfig`, consistent with drive editors having been renamed to apps. The `PHDocumentEditorConfig` names in the doc are still correct. Some doc comments in source also lag, describing `setPHAppConfig` as \"the global drive config\".\n\n_Source: packages/reactor-browser/src/types/config.ts, src/hooks/config/set-config-by-object.ts and packages/codegen/src/templates/app/editor.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45); the academy's React Hooks page still uses the removed setPHDriveEditorConfig names._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:38:08.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:38:09.499Z"
    }
  },
